@model SettingsViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Settings";
}
<div class="data-banner"><strong>ADMINISTRATOR SETTINGS</strong><span>Read-only production-readiness controls and effective backend boundaries.</span></div>
<section class="settings-grid">
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">DEPLOYMENT TOPOLOGY</span><h3>HA readiness guard</h3></div></div><label>Configured mode<div class="fake-input">@Model.Deployment.Mode <span>@Model.Deployment.Status</span></div></label><label>Multi-node readiness<div class="fake-input">@(Model.Deployment.Mode == Monitor.Web.Services.DeploymentTopology.MultiNode ? "Requested" : "Cross-field gate armed") <span>@(Model.Deployment.Ready ? "Safe for selected mode" : "Blocked")</span></div></label><p>@Model.Deployment.Message</p><div class="lab-rule state-warning"><span>!</span><div><strong>Node-local state still present</strong><p>@string.Join(" · ", Model.Deployment.NodeLocalState)</p></div></div></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SHARED STATE</span><h3>Dedicated Monitor state provider</h3></div></div><label>Provider<div class="fake-input">@Model.SharedState.Provider <span>@Model.SharedState.Status</span></div></label><label>Schema<div class="fake-input">@(Model.SharedState.SchemaVersion?.ToString() ?? "Not available") <span>Required v1</span></div></label><label>Shared storage capability<div class="fake-input">@(Model.SharedState.SharedStorageReady ? "READY" : "NOT READY") <span>Monitor-owned DB only</span></div></label><p>@Model.SharedState.Message</p><small>Provider endpoint and credentials are intentionally omitted. Shared repositories and distributed leases may use this provider, while the deployment gate continues to block MultiNode until every remaining node-local security/cache dependency has an approved strategy.</small></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">COLLECTION</span><h3>Snapshot policy</h3></div></div><label>Monitoring GET behavior<div class="fake-input">Cache Peek only <span>Zero SQL</span></div></label><label>Manual refresh<div class="fake-input">Operator/Admin POST <span>Distributed single-flight capable</span></div></label><p>Browser navigation reads cached monitored-SQL evidence only. Coordination traffic targets the separate Monitor-owned state database and never a monitored target.</p></article>
    <article class="glass-panel settings-card"><div class="panel-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SECURITY</span><h3>Credential boundaries</h3></div></div><label>Development Admin<div class="fake-input">PBKDF2-SHA256 hash <span>120k iterations</span></div></label><label>SQL Login secrets<div class="fake-input">Protected local store <span>Data Protection</span></div></label><p>Protected SQL Login credentials and the Data Protection key ring remain node-local in Batch 1. The HA gate therefore remains fail-closed for MultiNode until the security-state batch externalizes or prohibits those local dependencies.</p></article>
</section>
